I wrote the obituary spec in `.kiro/specs/obituary/` as `requirements.md` (EARS, REQ-1 to REQ-9), `design.md` and `tasks.md` (15 tasks in 5 batches). It follows the format of the revenant-watch spec. I changed no code and ran no tests. I did not check the review's measured numbers (the 76/80/68/56% shares, the 17 of 77 reverts, the 1,595 links) against the graveyard JSON. They are quoted as given.

Choices I made where the review was open or ambiguous:

- **Missing obituaries:** your item 3 says "say nothing new" and your last line says "say so". The spec says nothing when no obituary file exists, so all output stays byte-identical. Once a file exists, `check` and `get_tombstone` print `obituary: not fetched` or `obituary: none found on GitHub (looked up <date>)`. The hook, the Stop message, `check_snippet` and the web ghost card stay silent.
- **Reasons for blocking:** a link still counts as a reason without an obituary, so existing levels don't drop. The rule is a Revert, or any link, or obituary text. Titles alone don't count. The strict reading, where a bare `#N` no longer counts, is open question 1 in `design.md`.
- **Revert detection:** one function, `isRevertSubject`, in `src/core/revert.ts`. It matches `^\s*revert(s|ed|ing)?\b` case-insensitively on the first line.
  - `revival-tracker` currently uses a case-sensitive `startsWith('Revert')`. That is a third variant, and it moves to the shared function.
  - Existing graveyards change as a result, so Task 1 measures the effect on the 6 repos first, in line with the evidence-first rule.
  - A source-scan test forbids any other revert regex.
- **Obituary file:** it is a sidecar, `.deja-boo/obituaries.json`, attached to tombstones in memory. It is not written into `graveyard.json` or `causeOfDeath`, so `index` stays offline and deterministic. The file is git-ignored like the graveyard.
- **Re-runs:** a commit with no PR is stored as `pr: null`, so a re-run doesn't spend requests on it again. Errors aren't stored, so they get retried. Existing entries are kept, and only missing commits are fetched.
- **Extra field:** I added `truncated: boolean` to the entry shape. That lets the display add `…` outside the quotes while the stored excerpt stays verbatim.
- **Fetch order:** `--limit` counts distinct death commits. Alive-at-HEAD tombstones that aren't Reverts are skipped.
- **Link kinds:** `Link.type` gains `'ref'` for a bare `#N`. Close-keyword references (`fixes #N`) stay `issue`. Links are deduplicated by `ref`, and bare links get `<repoUrl>/issues/N`.
- **Untrusted text:** PR bodies are third-party text that will reach agents through the hook and MCP. The spec has formatters print them in quotes after a fixed label, and Task 15 adds a line to the skill telling the agent to treat them as data.
- **Rate limit:** the command stops cleanly, writes what it has and exits 0. A missing graveyard exits 3 and a missing repo exits 1.

